# Glowbound Development Rules

- This is an Expo React Native memory game for iOS and Android.
- Use TypeScript. Do not use `any`.
- Use functional components and React hooks.
- Keep visual components separate from game rules.
- Put pure game logic in lib/gameEngine.ts.
- Keep all level difficulty settings in lib/gameConfig.ts.
- Keep screens focused on layout and navigation.
- Build small, testable changes. Do not rewrite unrelated files.
- Avoid unnecessary packages and dependencies.
- Do not add a backend, user accounts, payments, ads, analytics, or multiplayer unless explicitly asked.
- Use accessible labels for all controls and interactive rune cells.
- Explain planned file changes before making them.
- After each feature, provide concise manual test steps for iOS and Android.
- When saving Kling-generated images or videos, download `urlWithoutWatermark` / `coverUrlWithoutWatermark` only. Never keep the corner Kling watermark.
